---
/**
 * /terms/ (WEB-FEAT-013, WEB-DEC-029). The app's terms of use (app repo web/terms.html,
 * effective 25 September 2026) in the site layout, plus the website's own part (section 12).
 * Wording kept from the app except: one sentence re-worded to avoid a banned word
 * (CONTENT_GUIDE.md §11) with the same meaning, and the website sections. /terms.html 301s here.
 * Company details: owner item 9 (placeholders on a preview build; production refuses to build).
 */
import DocPage from '../../components/trust/DocPage.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import { companyForBuild } from '../../lib/legal-page';

const company = companyForBuild();
const path = '/terms/';
const brand = site.brand;
const updated = '4 October 2026';

const toc = [
  { id: 'what', label: '1. What PalmSays does' },
  { id: 'reflection', label: '2. Reflection only' },
  { id: 'who', label: '3. Who may use it' },
  { id: 'account', label: '4. Your account' },
  { id: 'free', label: '5. Free readings' },
  { id: 'subscriptions', label: '6. Subscriptions' },
  { id: 'packs', label: '7. Reading packs' },
  { id: 'refunds', label: '8. Refunds' },
  { id: 'fair', label: '9. Using it fairly' },
  { id: 'content', label: '10. Content and ownership' },
  { id: 'delete', label: '11. Deleting your account' },
  { id: 'website', label: '12. The website' },
  { id: 'changes', label: '13. Changes' },
  { id: 'liability', label: '14. Liability' },
  { id: 'law', label: '15. Law and disputes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: '16. Contact' },
];

const webpage = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': `${site.baseUrl}${path}#webpage`,
  name: `${brand} terms of use`,
  url: `${site.baseUrl}${path}`,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  dateModified: '2026-10-04',
  publisher: { '@id': `${site.baseUrl}/#organization` },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of use | ${brand}`}
  description={`The rules for the ${brand} app and website: reflection only, 18+, free readings, subscriptions and packs through Google Play, refunds and your account.`}
  path={path}
  locale="en"
  jsonLd={[webpage]}
>
  <DocPage
    crumb="Terms of use"
    path={path}
    icon="book"
    kicker="Terms"
    title="Terms of use"
    lead={`The agreement between you and the operator of ${brand}, in plain words: what the app and website do, what they can't do, and how buying and deleting work.`}
    meta={`${brand} is operated by ${company.name}${company.location ? `, ${company.location}` : ''}. Effective ${updated}.`}
    toc={toc}
  >
    <p>
      These terms are an agreement between you and {company.name}{company.location ? `, ${company.location}` : ''} ("we", "us"), an
      individual who operates the {brand} app and the {site.domain} website. By using them you accept these terms. Please also read our <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>,
      which explains what data {brand} uses and how you delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what">1. What {brand} does</h2>
    <p>
      {brand} looks at a photograph of your palm, traces the major lines it can see, and gives a traditional Indian palmistry
      interpretation of them. It also has short lessons and guides about palmistry. Where a line cannot be seen clearly, it says so
      instead of guessing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="reflection">2. Reflection and entertainment only</h2>
    <p>
      Traditional palmistry interpretation, for reflection and entertainment. Not scientifically established, not prediction, and never
      medical, financial or legal advice.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A reading never gives a date or a promised outcome, and you should not treat it as one.</li>
      <li>Do not make health, money, legal, relationship or other important decisions based on a reading. For those, speak to a qualified professional.</li>
      <li>{brand} can misread a photo: lines can be missed, confused or measured imperfectly.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="who">3. Who may use it</h2>
    <p>
      You must be {site.ageRule} or older to use {brand}. By using it you confirm that you are. If we learn that an account belongs to
      someone under {site.ageRule}, we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="account">4. Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You can start without signing up; {brand} then uses a random guest account on your device. You can add an email address or sign
      in with Google so your readings and purchases survive a new phone. The same account works in the app and on the website. Keep
      your sign-in details to yourself; you are responsible for what happens in your account.
    </p>

    <h2 id="free">5. Free readings</h2>
    <p>
      {brand} offers a small number of free readings, and shows before you start what a free reading includes (at present some parts of
      a free reading are open in full and the others are shown as a preview). We may change the free offer for future readings; a
      change never takes back a reading you already received. Trying to get extra free readings, for example with made-up accounts, is
      not allowed.
    </p>

    <h2 id="subscriptions">6. Subscriptions (Palm Read Pro)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Subscriptions are optional. They are sold and billed by Google Play, under Google Play's terms, in your Google Play account. We never see your card or UPI details.</li>
      <li>Each plan gives a set number of readings in each billing month, shown before you buy. Unused readings in a month do not carry over.</li>
      <li>A subscription renews automatically at the end of each period, at the price Google Play showed you, until you cancel.</li>
      <li>If a plan starts with a free trial and you do not cancel before the trial ends, Google Play charges the plan price and the subscription continues. The trial's terms, including how many readings it gives, are shown before you start it.</li>
      <li>You can cancel at any time in the Google Play Store app: Profile, then Payments and subscriptions, then Subscriptions. After cancelling you keep the subscription until the end of the period you paid for.</li>
      <li>Deleting the app or your {brand} account does <strong>not</strong> cancel a subscription. Cancel it in Google Play.</li>
      <li>A report you opened in full while subscribed stays open after the subscription ends.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="packs">7. One-time reading packs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A reading pack is a one-time purchase of a set number of readings, sold and billed by Google Play.</li>
      <li>Readings from a pack do not expire. They belong to the {brand} account that bought them, cannot be transferred, and have no cash value.</li>
      <li>When you have both, a new reading uses a pack reading before a free one, so a paid reading is always complete. An active subscription's monthly readings are used before pack readings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="refunds">8. Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      Payments go through Google Play, so refunds follow Google Play's refund policy; you can request one from Google Play. If something
      went wrong (for example you were charged but did not receive your readings) write to us and we will help put it right. Nothing in
      these terms takes away any right you have under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 or other law that applies to you. The steps are
      in our <a class="text-link" href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="fair">9. Using {brand} fairly</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Photograph only your own palm, or the palm of another adult who has agreed to it.</li>
      <li>Do not use a reading to judge, pressure or make decisions about another person, for example in hiring, marriage or lending.</li>
      <li>Do not upload photos that are not of a hand, or that are unlawful or someone else's private images.</li>
      <li>Do not copy, resell or scrape the app, the website or their content, try to get around their limits or security, or interfere with their servers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may suspend an account that breaks these rules, and will tell you why where we can.</p>

    <h2 id="content">10. Content and ownership</h2>
    <p>
      Your palm photo is yours. You let us use it only to produce your reading, as the privacy policy describes; no server keeps it. The
      app and website, their design, the interpretation texts and the wording of readings belong to us or our licensors (see Licences
      and credits in the app). You may save and share your own reports for personal, non-commercial use.
    </p>

    <h2 id="delete">11. Deleting your account</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time: in the app (Profile, then Delete my account) or on the web at <a class="text-link" href="/delete-account/">{site.domain}/delete-account/</a>. Deleting it removes your readings, and any unused
      pack readings are lost; this cannot be undone. Remember to cancel any subscription in Google Play separately.
    </p>

    <h2 id="website">12. The website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The guides and tools on {site.domain} are free to read and use, with no account. They follow the same rule as the app: reflection, not prediction.</li>
      <li>The photo tools measure your hand on your own device; their results are rough, can be wrong, and depend on the photo.</li>
      <li>Nothing is sold on the website. When the website reading is open, it offers only free readings, and our server decides how many are left; paid readings are in the Android app.</li>
      <li>Links to Google Play and other sites lead to services with their own terms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="changes">13. Changes and availability</h2>
    <p>
      We keep improving {brand}, so features, plans and the free offer can change. If we change these terms in a way that matters, the
      app will tell you, and this page will say so, before the change applies. We try to keep {brand} available but cannot promise it
      will always work without interruption.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">14. Limits on our liability</h2>
    <p>
      {brand} is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, we are not responsible for decisions you make based on a reading, or
      for indirect or consequential loss. Where we are responsible, our total liability to you is limited to the amount you paid us in
      the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2 id="law">15. Law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of India. If you have a complaint, please write to us first so we can try to resolve it.
      Disputes are subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of India, without affecting your right to approach a consumer commission.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">16. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, complaints or refund problems: <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Grievance Officer: {company.grievanceOfficer}, <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>. We
      acknowledge every complaint within {site.grievanceTimes.acknowledgeHours} hours and resolve it within {site.grievanceTimes.resolveDays} days of receiving it.
    </p>
    <p>Operator: {company.name}{company.location ? `, ${company.location}` : ''} (an individual, not a company).</p>
  </DocPage>
</BaseLayout>
